# Findings of the image scan that are accepted for now, each with the reason and a date to look at it again.
# Everything else with a fix available fails the build (see .github/workflows/ci.yml, job docker-build).

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19: fixed only in 7.0.9 (Spring Framework 7 / Spring Boot 4); there is no fix in the 6.2 line.
# CVE-2026-47884: remote code execution through XsltView path handling. This application serves JSON and has no XSLT view.
# CVE-2026-47890: corrupted Server-Sent Events streams with views. This application does not stream SSE through views.
# Real fix: move to Spring Boot 4, a project of its own.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2026-12-31

# minio-java 8.5.17 (CVE-2025-59952, fixed in 8.6.0): the client could be made to read a wrong value from an XML answer of the
# S3 server. The only server this application talks to is its own MinIO. Version 8.6.0 is built on OkHttp 5 and was not taken
# because it could not be tried against a real MinIO here (the image is no longer pullable from the registries reachable from
# the development machine); S3BlobStoreMinioTest is ready for that and runs when BC_TEST_MINIO_ENDPOINT is set.
CVE-2025-59952 exp:2026-12-31

# /usr/bin/pebble: a Go binary that belongs to the base image (eclipse-temurin:21-jre), not to this project; this
# application never starts it. Fixed by a new build of the base image; the image is rebuilt on every release.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-12-31
